**R** can be used to make a polymer, **W**, in two steps.

{{figure:pdf_visual_02.png}}

Draw one repeat unit of **W**.

In the first step, **Z** reacts with $\text{HBr}$ to form two products. The structure of the product depends on which intermediate is formed, intermediate **I** or intermediate **II**.

{{figure:pdf_visual_03.png}}

Explain why intermediate **I** is more likely to form than intermediate **II**.

When intermediate **I** forms, the product of the first step is **T**.

Complete the diagram to show the mechanism for the conversion of **Z** to **T**. Include all relevant charges, partial charges, curly arrows and lone pairs.

{{figure:pdf_visual_04.png}}

**T** can then be converted to 2-aminopropane.

{{figure:pdf_visual_05.png}}

Name the mechanism for this conversion.
